<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Birkenfeld</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Birkenfeld is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hunsruck">Hunsrück</a> hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Once part of the County of Sponheim, it was from 1569 the seat of the Palatinate-Birkenfeld line of the Wittelsbachs. In 1817 its district became the Principality of Birkenfeld, an exclave of Oldenburg, until it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-hamburg-act">Greater Hamburg Act</a> of 1937.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/birkenfeld.jpg" alt="Birkenfeld" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Blueduck4711 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Birkenfeld-nahe-vom-burgberg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
